															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/amendment50" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198313); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2198313&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606447554" alt="Amendment50" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2198313)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/amendment50" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198313); return false;" >Amendment50</a></span> <span class="odate time_1436041039 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jul 2015 20:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2331213">
									

<p>I'm brand new myself, so I don't want to act like an expert, but this is very well-written in my opinion. It just has the right tone to it- clinical and sort of dry, describing it in terms that are painstakingly specific and yet somehow make it feel sort of vague. I get the impression you were very meticulous in making this read a certain way. This is the sort of thing people have conspiracy theories about, I think. Earned my upvote.</p>
<p>Aside from that, my one question is, why the Euclid classification? Seems like a craft made out of antimatter that could have &quot;catastrophic consequences&quot; on containment breach and has to be stored on the goddamn MOON should be classified as a Keter.</p>

							</div>

								
					
