														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2331434">
									

<p>Thanks! I'm glad you liked it.</p>
<p>The idea is that the craft, despite its hazardous composition, can be contained indefinitely. It's out of fuel, so there isn't anything the creature inside it can do to breach containment. Even if the power went offline and both backup reactors failed and the field generators turned off and the craft contacted the interior of the containment unit, it would just cause an explosion. A gargantuan explosion, but still just an explosion. And that would be it. One boom. It's just stored on the Moon because transporting it to the Earth's surface would involve unnecessary risk.</p>
<p>I think that would make it Safe. The reason it's Euclid is because of the dude inside it.</p>
<p>Eventually, when the poor guy comes out of suspended animation and starves to death, it could probably be downgraded to Safe.</p>

							</div>

								
