			<div class="content" id="post-content-2333395">
									

<p>Given the foundation's budget and some near-future technology 1kT's totally doable.</p>
<p>We've built 1&#160;kT+ electromagnets, but they only work at a burst because you have to keep them cool while pumping a huge amount of power through them. The largest such device is the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z_Pulsed_Power_Facility">z-pulsed power facility</a>, aka the Z-machine, aka the closest thing to <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WaveMotionGun">a wave motion gun</a> mankind has yet built. (In addition to being used for studying fusion reactions and generating massive magnetic fields and X-ray beams, it can shoot small metal plates at 3x escape velocity 8D) <a href="http://www.photographsofthewest.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/08/NationalGeo_1252741.png">Also, this is what the z-machine looks like in operation.</a> It has been scientifically proven to be one of the most unrelentingly awesome machines ever constructed.</p>
<p>Anyway, you'd need one of these, but replacing the tungsten wire arrays with a highish temperature superconductor, and hooked up to something like a fusion reactor. But yeah, doable without dragging out too much magitek.</p>

